From 2c48444af102006c6b4d6248ca1217489c5d3bbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stuart <stuart@local>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:55:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] helios_exec: per-system sizing (exec.sizing) and the demo
 spread bet account
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stuart decides the size at each step, per system: exec.sizing holds a fixed £/pt
stake or a system's own £ per R; anything without a row uses the warehouse target.
H43 VIX is set to a fixed £4/pt.

IG demo logins hold a spread bet and a CFD account. The demo session now switches
to the spread bet account (or HX_IG_ACCOUNT_ID if set) and the broker refuses to
trade on a CFD account, since the systems' markets are DFB spread bets. The run
log says which account it used.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PaJF5erxAsVSeLZKZmj7PD
